---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

// FINAL: Terms v6, adopted 10–0 on 2026-11-17 (file SHA-256 0d21a91b…ce37). Word for word; change it only with
// Christian's approval.
const email = site.contactEmail;
const mail = `mailto:${email}`;
---

<Layout title="terms" description="The terms for using Cueory.">
  <Prose>
    <h1>terms of use</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated 17 November 2026</p>

    <p>
      Cueory is a free study site for nursing students. An individual in Arizona, USA, owns and runs it. In these terms,
      “Cueory,” “we” and “us” mean that owner. Please read these terms and the <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> before
      using the site. Use Cueory only if you agree to both.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can use Cueory</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 16. If you are at least 16 and still a minor where you live, a parent or legal guardian must
      read these terms with you and agree to them before you use Cueory.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has shared
      personal information with us, email <a href={mail}>{email}</a>. Please leave sensitive details out of your first
      message. If we learn we have collected personal information from a child under 13, we will promptly delete it from
      our records and ask any provider holding it for us to do the same, except where the law requires us to keep it.
    </p>

    <h2>What you can use today</h2>
    <p>
      You can try sample study activities and daily puzzles without an account. Some pages are placeholders. Public
      account registration has not opened. You can join the launch email list through the “get launch updates” email box
      (on the home page and in the signup pop-up), which sends your address straight to Kit, or through Cueory’s signup
      page on Kit. You can send feedback by email to <a href={mail}>{email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cueory is free to use. If we introduce a charge for access, we’ll announce it on the site before it takes effect. We
      may change, pause or discontinue a feature.
    </p>

    <h2>Using and sharing study materials</h2>
    <p>
      You may use our materials for personal, noncommercial study, including taking notes and printing study materials
      for yourself. Cueory or its licensors own the site’s content, name, logo and design. If material carries a separate
      license, that license governs its use. These terms preserve uses permitted by law.
    </p>
    <p>These rules apply when you use Cueory.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Get our written permission before selling, republishing or distributing our materials beyond the uses allowed
        above.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keep confidential or unreleased exam material off Cueory and out of messages to us. This includes school and
        licensing exam questions or answers you remember from a test.
      </li>
      <li>Do not interfere with the site, overload it, bypass its security or use bots to collect its content in bulk.</li>
      <li>
        Do not send unlawful or harmful material, anyone else’s private information, or information about a real patient.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may limit or block access for violations of these terms.</p>

    <h2>Feedback and copyright concerns</h2>
    <p>
      To report a mistake, send the page title or link and a short description to <a href={mail}>{email}</a>. Leave out
      patient details and confidential exam material. If you send an idea or correction, we may use it to improve Cueory
      without paying you. You keep any rights you have in what you send.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe something on Cueory infringes your copyright, email us at the same address. Identify your work, link
      to the material on Cueory, tell us how to reach you and say whether you own the rights or represent the owner.
      We’ll review the report and remove material when appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>Other services and optional tips</h2>
    <p>
      Cueory links to YouTube and our other social media pages. If you choose to use an outside service, its terms and
      privacy policy also apply. Our launch email list is run by Kit: the email box sends your address straight to Kit,
      and Kit’s terms and privacy policy apply when you sign up. You must be at least 16 to join.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ko-fi requires users to be at least 18, so please tip only if you are 18 or older. If you choose to tip through
      Ko-fi, the tip goes to Cueory through a payment provider. A tip is optional and gives you no extra access. For a
      mistaken tip or a refund request, email <a href={mail}>{email}</a>.
      <a href="https://more.ko-fi.com/terms" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ko-fi’s terms</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      For information about data on your device and how we handle personal information, see the
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Warranties and limits on liability</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Cueory is provided “as is” and “as available.” To the extent the law allows, we disclaim express and implied
      warranties, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We
      cannot promise that the site will always be available, secure, accurate, complete or up to date.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>To the extent the law allows, Cueory and the people who help run it are not liable for indirect, incidental,
      special, consequential or punitive damages arising from use of the site, or for lost data, lost income or losses
      related to grades or exam results. For other claims arising from use of the site, the combined total liability of
      Cueory and the people who help run it to you, across all claims, is limited to US $50.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      These limits and disclaimers do not apply to fraud, intentional misconduct or gross negligence. You keep any rights
      or remedies that the law does not allow you to give up.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We’ll post changes on this page and update the date. For an important change, we’ll also post a notice on the site
      explaining the change and its effective date at least 14 days in advance. Other changes apply when posted. Changes
      apply to future use and do not affect claims arising before the change takes effect. We’ll ask for your agreement
      when the law requires it. If you disagree with an update, stop using Cueory once it takes effect.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law and agreement</h2>
    <p>
      Arizona law governs these terms, without regard to its conflict-of-law rules. Disputes arising from these terms or
      your use of Cueory belong in a state or federal court with jurisdiction in Maricopa County, Arizona. You keep any
      mandatory protections and any right to bring a claim elsewhere that the law where you live gives you.
    </p>
    <p>
      These terms and the Disclaimer are the entire agreement about your use of Cueory. If a court finds one part
      unenforceable, the rest still applies. If we do not enforce a term right away, we may still enforce it later.
    </p>
    <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href={mail}>{email}</a>.</p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
